	(text "Fixed 3.3 V; FB to AGND per datasheet. FSW low (2.5 MHz), 2.2 uH, 2x22 uF (table 9-1).\nSS 3.3 nF (typical application). PG_3V3 releases the 1.2 V and 3.3 V analog rails.\nWorst case 3.221-3.396 V (power-save mode, SLVSAG7F p5) inside VDDIO 3.14-3.47 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 195.284 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1e1a9c98-82b2-5ba2-9930-7b1affe49c61")
	)
	(text "5 V -> 3.3 V DIGITAL (TPS62133, 3 A)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 119.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "24b0edb5-1d77-5388-ab1d-7324ba6cbaec")
	)
	(text "5 V -> 3.3 V ANALOG (TPS7A2033)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 207.784 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5773110b-125c-50c3-9a41-f5dce55846cf")
	)
	(text "VOUT = 0.8 V x (1 + 5.23k/10.0k) = 1.218 V (eq. 6), 0.1 % 10 ppm/K: worst case 1.1872-1.2558 V\n(power-save VFB 781.6-822.4 mV, FB leakage, 0.1 % line/load) inside VDD 1.14-1.26 V (CSR-01).\nEnabled by PG_3V3: VDD rises after VDDIO (SPRSP14E table 7-1). VDD bulk on the decoupling sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 194.284 195.284 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "73b1d00f-7ff6-50c3-8ce1-446ff189cead")
	)
	(text "5 V -> 1.2 V CORE (TPS62130, 3 A)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 194.284 119.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "87bfacf5-c6a5-5b44-aec1-441ac4a38ed3")
	)
	(text "Table 9-1 row 400 kHz / 5 V / 2 A: L 15 uH, 3x22 uF, RFBT 100k / RFBB 24.9k -> 5.02 V, RT 64.9k.\nLoad (calculated): 3.3 V 1.3 A + 1.2 V 0.48 A + 3.3 V analog 0.1 A -> about 1.2 A at 5 V.\nEN tied to VIN (datasheet allows). PG_5V enables the 3.3 V converter.\nOutput capacitance check (SNVSC40E, calculated): total on +5V = 3x22 + 2x10 + 1 + 0.3 = 87 uF nominal,\n96 uF at +10 %: 1.45x the 66 uF design value, inside the 9.2.2.5 limit (10x design or 1000 uF) -> no extra\nstability study required. Start-up: tSS 4.0 ms (8.3.9) -> 96 uF x 5.02 V / 4 ms = 0.12 A charge current,\ndownstream loads held off by the PG chain, << ILS-LIMIT 1.8 A min; OCP blanking 18 ms -> no hiccup.\nInductor: LMIN = 0.25 x 5 V / 400 kHz = 3.1 uH (eq. 11) < 15 uH; ripple 0.64-0.68 A at 21.6-26.4 V in\n(> 10 % of 2 A); peak 1.54 A (1.62 A at L -20 %) < IHS-LIMIT 2.6 A min < ISAT 5.55 A. Bode not measured."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 106.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "93336e98-e64e-5bcd-83de-522c3eec31df")
	)
	(text "24 V -> 5 V (LMR38020, 400 KHZ)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ea9ac702-b506-5648-90d1-8e57cdcf02dc")
	)
	(text "VDDA, op amps, reference, mux. Enabled by PG_3V3 so VDDA never leads VDDIO.\nLoad (calculated): 26 op-amp channels x 2.6 mA max + IDDA 15 mA + REF and its 4.2 mA load + VBIAS\n+ 12 open-input bias resistors to +3V3A (16 mA) = about 110 mA of 300 mA."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14 248.184 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f50e7219-a705-5d7b-a84d-15046f00114e")
	)
